1
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:04,546
PARK MINJAE'S LIST

2
00:00:04,630 --> 00:00:05,923
START DATING...

3
00:00:36,620 --> 00:00:40,958
BETWEEN STEPS

4
00:00:41,583 --> 00:00:43,835
CHARACTERS, PLACES, ORGANIZATIONS,
AND EVENTS IN THIS DRAMA ARE FICTITIOUS

5
00:00:43,919 --> 00:00:45,546
THIS DRAMA CONTAINS SENSITIVE CONTENT

6
00:00:46,922 --> 00:00:49,174
EPISODE 4

7
00:01:27,754 --> 00:01:28,755
Oh...

8
00:01:52,154 --> 00:01:53,447
Hey, Lim Youjin.

9
00:01:54,197 --> 00:01:57,159
Do you know what time it is?
Why the hell are you still in bed?

10
00:01:57,242 --> 00:01:58,660
Are you going to get up or not?

11
00:01:59,911 --> 00:02:01,079
Hey, you little brat.

12
00:02:01,663 --> 00:02:03,582
When your mother is making breakfast,

13
00:02:03,665 --> 00:02:07,919
the least you can do is get up on time
and be at the table

14
00:02:08,003 --> 00:02:11,256
if you can't help her out, okay?

15
00:02:11,340 --> 00:02:12,341
[loudly] Get up now!

16
00:02:14,635 --> 00:02:16,094
Hey, are you crying?

17
00:02:19,931 --> 00:02:21,767
What's wrong? Are you sick?

18
00:02:26,063 --> 00:02:27,564
You do feel a little warm.

19
00:02:28,982 --> 00:02:31,610
Mom! I think she has a fever.

20
00:02:41,536 --> 00:02:42,537
Hey.

21
00:02:43,372 --> 00:02:44,373
[Minjae] Yes?

22
00:02:44,456 --> 00:02:46,083
It's past 9 a.m. now.

23
00:02:46,166 --> 00:02:47,376
What?

24
00:02:47,959 --> 00:02:52,047
It's past 9 a.m.,
and Lim Youjin still isn't here.

25
00:02:53,131 --> 00:02:54,132
She's late.

26
00:02:55,467 --> 00:02:56,468
Oh...

27
00:02:58,804 --> 00:03:00,472
She's late, right?

28
00:03:04,309 --> 00:03:09,064
Is this lab pretty flexible
about what time people come in?

29
00:03:09,147 --> 00:03:12,025
Is it okay to come in at 10 or 11?
I'm just curious.

30
00:03:12,109 --> 00:03:13,777
No, we start at 9 a.m.

31
00:03:13,860 --> 00:03:14,903
[Sejin] Ah...

32
00:03:14,986 --> 00:03:17,406
I knew it. And yet she hasn't arrived.

33
00:03:18,573 --> 00:03:20,742
She's not late. It's just turned 9 a.m.

34
00:03:22,285 --> 00:03:23,704
Maybe the traffic's bad.

35
00:03:23,787 --> 00:03:26,790
If the traffic's bad,
she should've left earlier, right?

36
00:03:26,873 --> 00:03:28,792
She's keeping us waiting for our meeting.

37
00:03:29,960 --> 00:03:34,131
[clears throat] Then, should I call her?

38
00:03:35,006 --> 00:03:36,091
And see where she is?

39
00:03:36,967 --> 00:03:38,510
Sure, give her a call.

40
00:03:38,593 --> 00:03:39,928
[Sejin] All right, got it.

41
00:03:41,888 --> 00:03:44,766
Actually, no, Hangyeol,
could you call her and ask where she is?

42
00:03:46,435 --> 00:03:48,061
She'll get here when she gets here.

43
00:03:48,145 --> 00:03:50,021
As if rushing her will make a difference.

44
00:03:52,274 --> 00:03:54,609
See? She came.

45
00:03:54,693 --> 00:03:56,403
[Youjin] I'm sorry I'm late.

46
00:03:56,903 --> 00:03:58,697
Let's try to get to work on time, okay?

47
00:04:01,283 --> 00:04:03,910
Now that Youjin is here,
let's start the meeting.

48
00:04:05,078 --> 00:04:07,914
Did you all see the email Sejin sent?

49
00:04:07,998 --> 00:04:09,166
-Yes.
-Yes.

50
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:13,128
[Minjae] Sejin, how did you find the time
to put this all together?

51
00:04:13,211 --> 00:04:16,590
It's just... I just did it at home.

52
00:04:16,673 --> 00:04:18,967
It's only a draft, so it's pretty rough.

53
00:04:19,050 --> 00:04:20,051
[Minjae] No, it's not rough.

54
00:04:21,011 --> 00:04:23,054
You have really good instincts.

55
00:04:23,138 --> 00:04:25,098
This is right on point. Great job.

56
00:04:25,182 --> 00:04:26,349
It's nothing.

57
00:04:26,433 --> 00:04:30,061
No, honestly, I was a bit surprised too.
You did a great job.

58
00:04:30,145 --> 00:04:32,981
-[Minjae] Yeah.
-We've got a really talented rookie.

59
00:04:33,064 --> 00:04:36,651
But raising the TRL
within a short timeframe won't be easy.

60
00:04:36,735 --> 00:04:40,447
Either way, we'll need
to make a finite element analysis graph.

61
00:04:41,656 --> 00:04:43,867
So let's start thinking
about our approach.

62
00:04:43,950 --> 00:04:45,827
Who reviews the proposal, by the way?

63
00:04:46,703 --> 00:04:49,372
-Well, I suppose mostly senior members.
-[Minjae] Yeah.

64
00:04:49,456 --> 00:04:52,000
[Taeho] We need a trick here.

65
00:04:52,083 --> 00:04:55,295
The reviewers can't possibly
get through all 300, 400 pages anyway.

66
00:04:55,879 --> 00:04:59,674
So we need to make graphs that pop, okay?

67
00:04:59,758 --> 00:05:01,760
-[Minjae] Yeah.
-[Taeho] With lots of color.

68
00:05:01,843 --> 00:05:03,678
The key is to make it visually engaging.

69
00:05:03,762 --> 00:05:05,263
Right, then, I'll use RecurDyn--

70
00:05:05,347 --> 00:05:06,932
I can do that.

71
00:05:14,189 --> 00:05:18,318
You don't know
how to use RecurDyn, Ms. Lim.

72
00:05:20,153 --> 00:05:21,363
Um...

73
00:05:21,446 --> 00:05:24,157
Well, I've used Illustrator before,
for fashion design.

74
00:05:24,741 --> 00:05:26,993
-[Taeho] Hmm.
-[Sejin] I'd say they're different.

75
00:05:27,077 --> 00:05:29,496
How are they different?
They're similar, Mr. Kim.

76
00:05:30,872 --> 00:05:33,124
Youjin, do you think you can do it?

77
00:05:34,918 --> 00:05:35,919
Yes.

78
00:05:36,002 --> 00:05:38,463
All right. If you think you can do it,
give it a try.

79
00:05:38,547 --> 00:05:41,299
Feel free to ask us anytime
if you have any questions.

80
00:05:41,383 --> 00:05:42,384
Okay.

81
00:05:42,968 --> 00:05:46,429
[Taeho] By the way, there's something
that's been bothering me.

82
00:05:46,513 --> 00:05:48,473
-Uh...
-[Minjae] Mmm... Sure, what is it?

83
00:05:48,557 --> 00:05:50,517
What are those sneakers?

84
00:05:50,600 --> 00:05:52,185
I haven't seen them before.

85
00:05:52,269 --> 00:05:53,270
[Minjae] These?

86
00:05:53,353 --> 00:05:56,857
Wait, pink?
Men's sneakers come in pink too?

87
00:05:56,940 --> 00:05:58,942
-Did you buy them?
-[Taeho chuckles]

88
00:05:59,025 --> 00:06:01,194
They were a birthday gift.

89
00:06:01,278 --> 00:06:02,487
Youjin gave them to me.

90
00:06:03,488 --> 00:06:07,784
Unlike you guys, who didn't get
your esteemed senior a cookie crumb.

91
00:06:07,868 --> 00:06:13,415
Anyway, our rookies are cute,
hardworking, and sweet. I love it.

92
00:06:13,498 --> 00:06:15,667
[Taeho] Ah... It's a birthday gift.

93
00:06:16,167 --> 00:06:19,629
Wow, but that's really nice of her.
I'm moved.

94
00:06:19,713 --> 00:06:20,714
-I know, right?
-Yeah.

95
00:06:20,797 --> 00:06:23,258
No wonder.
Those sneakers are growing on me.

96
00:06:23,341 --> 00:06:24,342
[Taeho] Yeah.

97
00:06:24,426 --> 00:06:26,636
Seriously, that was such a good choice.

98
00:06:26,720 --> 00:06:28,805
-[Minjae] Pretty cute, right?
-Pink is a man's color.

99
00:06:28,889 --> 00:06:30,599
-Great choice, Youjin.
-[Minjae] They're nice.

100
00:06:30,682 --> 00:06:33,351
[Sejin] By the way, Minjae,
your prosthetic leg is titanium, right?

101
00:06:33,435 --> 00:06:35,478
[Minjae] Ah... Yeah.

102
00:06:36,062 --> 00:06:38,899
Titanium is lightweight and strong.

103
00:06:38,982 --> 00:06:42,944
Actually, I came across this paper
on a new material.

104
00:06:43,028 --> 00:06:46,531
Really? If you come across anything
like that, just send it my way.

105
00:06:46,615 --> 00:06:47,824
-[Sejin] Okay.
-[Minjae] Yeah.

106
00:06:47,908 --> 00:06:50,201
[inhales] Anyway, Youjin,
thanks for these.

107
00:06:50,910 --> 00:06:51,911
Thank you.

108
00:07:14,059 --> 00:07:15,060
[Minjae] Hey.

109
00:07:16,645 --> 00:07:18,104
Why were you late today?

110
00:07:19,814 --> 00:07:20,815
Um...

111
00:07:21,691 --> 00:07:23,068
I wasn't feeling well.

112
00:07:23,735 --> 00:07:26,321
My head was hurting,
and my stomach was hurting too.

113
00:07:26,946 --> 00:07:28,198
[Minjae] Did you go to the doctor?

114
00:07:29,366 --> 00:07:32,202
No, I took some medicine,
and I got better.

115
00:07:32,285 --> 00:07:33,286
[Minjae] Hmm.

116
00:07:33,787 --> 00:07:35,288
You do look a little puffy.

117
00:07:35,955 --> 00:07:37,916
-No, I'm not.
-[Minjae] Never mind, then.

118
00:07:41,127 --> 00:07:42,837
Well, you weren't feeling well,

119
00:07:44,589 --> 00:07:46,383
so I can't be too hard on you for that.

120
00:07:46,466 --> 00:07:48,885
But we were supposed to meet
at 9 a.m. today,

121
00:07:48,968 --> 00:07:51,846
and you shouldn't
have kept everyone waiting.

122
00:07:52,972 --> 00:07:53,973
Right?

123
00:07:54,516 --> 00:07:57,977
As a newbie, the least you could do
was show up early and be prepared.

124
00:08:00,814 --> 00:08:01,815
Don't be late.

125
00:08:02,774 --> 00:08:04,651
-[Minjae sighs]
-I'm sorry.

126
00:08:07,112 --> 00:08:08,113
What?

127
00:08:08,196 --> 00:08:09,739
I have something to tell you.

128
00:08:11,324 --> 00:08:12,325
[Minjae] What is it?

129
00:08:14,077 --> 00:08:16,538
Can we step outside for a second?

130
00:08:18,331 --> 00:08:19,416
You can tell me here.

131
00:08:22,168 --> 00:08:23,628
[Youjin] It's kind of personal.

132
00:08:24,879 --> 00:08:28,675
Do we have anything personal
to talk about?

133
00:08:29,509 --> 00:08:32,220
Well, it's not like it's some big secret,
is it? [chuckles awkwardly]

134
00:08:32,762 --> 00:08:34,889
Just tell me. I'm curious.

135
00:08:46,401 --> 00:08:49,320
-Do you really want me to say it here?
-Yeah, go ahead.

136
00:08:49,988 --> 00:08:51,156
Why not?

137
00:08:56,870 --> 00:08:58,538
What I did that day was wrong.

138
00:08:59,372 --> 00:09:01,416
Wrong? What was wrong?

139
00:09:03,752 --> 00:09:05,462
I was in the wrong from the start.

140
00:09:06,671 --> 00:09:08,757
I shouldn't have shown up unannounced,

141
00:09:10,300 --> 00:09:12,635
and I shouldn't have given you
those shoes either.

142
00:09:16,014 --> 00:09:20,477
I just couldn't believe it at the time,
so I wanted to see it for myself.

143
00:09:23,938 --> 00:09:25,607
And I just left like that...

144
00:09:27,609 --> 00:09:30,403
because I was so caught off guard
I didn't know what to do.

145
00:09:34,449 --> 00:09:36,951
I'm sorry I hurt you like that.

146
00:09:39,079 --> 00:09:41,039
[Minjae] Then you have nothing
to apologize for.

147
00:09:42,582 --> 00:09:44,084
I wasn't hurt.

148
00:09:47,420 --> 00:09:49,380
Actually, I'm the one
who should apologize.

149
00:09:51,049 --> 00:09:56,221
For not being the person
you thought I was.

150
00:09:57,263 --> 00:10:01,392
And that made you sad,
caught you off guard, and made you angry.

151
00:10:04,020 --> 00:10:05,063
I'm sorry.

152
00:10:11,486 --> 00:10:14,823
Now that we've both apologized,
why don't we call it a day a little early?

153
00:10:15,406 --> 00:10:16,783
-Sejin!
-[Sejin] Yes?

154
00:10:18,034 --> 00:10:20,787
[Minjae] Mmm... If you're
pretty much done, you can head home now.

155
00:10:21,663 --> 00:10:23,915
[Sejin] Okay.
I was about to leave, actually.

156
00:10:24,707 --> 00:10:25,959
[Minjae] Good work, everyone.

157
00:10:26,751 --> 00:10:27,836
Good work today.

158
00:10:28,503 --> 00:10:29,754
See you tomorrow.

159
00:10:49,691 --> 00:10:50,900
Hey...

160
00:10:52,527 --> 00:10:53,903
When you left earlier...

161
00:10:54,904 --> 00:10:56,364
When you left the lab earlier...

162
00:10:56,865 --> 00:11:00,368
-[Sejin] Yes.
-Was Youjin crying?

163
00:11:02,704 --> 00:11:04,747
I mean, did she look like she was?

164
00:11:06,374 --> 00:11:08,042
She didn't look like
she was crying, but...

165
00:11:08,126 --> 00:11:09,127
[Minjae] Yes.

166
00:11:09,669 --> 00:11:10,712
She seemed...

167
00:11:12,839 --> 00:11:14,465
a bit pissed off.

168
00:11:58,343 --> 00:11:59,636
By the way...

169
00:12:03,181 --> 00:12:05,308
What was Lim Youjin talking about earlier?

170
00:12:07,477 --> 00:12:09,187
-What?
-Did something happen?

171
00:12:11,314 --> 00:12:12,315
Oh...

172
00:12:12,815 --> 00:12:16,861
Well, I didn't mean to listen in
or anything... [inhales sharply]

173
00:12:16,945 --> 00:12:19,239
...but I happened to overhear a little.

174
00:12:22,992 --> 00:12:26,663
By the way, what's up with you and Youjin?

175
00:12:27,497 --> 00:12:28,623
[Sejin] Hmm?

176
00:12:28,706 --> 00:12:30,959
Might as well
try to get along with your cohort.

177
00:12:33,836 --> 00:12:36,547
I mean, you'll be working together
for at least two years,

178
00:12:36,631 --> 00:12:38,341
and maybe for the rest of your life.

179
00:12:38,424 --> 00:12:40,426
So why not just get along?

180
00:12:43,596 --> 00:12:46,349
She keeps acting selfish
and getting on my nerves.

181
00:12:47,600 --> 00:12:51,229
Hey, what do you mean, she's selfish
and getting on your nerves? When?

182
00:12:53,648 --> 00:12:55,733
Maybe you don't like
certain things about her,

183
00:12:55,817 --> 00:12:58,987
but why don't you try
to give a little too, you know?

184
00:13:00,196 --> 00:13:02,031
But she doesn't give an inch either.

185
00:13:02,865 --> 00:13:04,909
So why should I? Because she's a woman?

186
00:13:04,993 --> 00:13:08,788
No, not because she's a woman,
but as her colleague and her friend.

187
00:13:09,497 --> 00:13:12,458
Sometimes, you can just give in
and let her have her way.

188
00:13:13,751 --> 00:13:14,752
Huh?

189
00:13:16,379 --> 00:13:17,880
Forget it. Bye.

190
00:13:18,506 --> 00:13:19,507
Hey.

191
00:13:23,052 --> 00:13:25,680
If you're having dinner soon,
do you want to eat together?

192
00:13:25,763 --> 00:13:27,015
I can order us something.

193
00:13:28,474 --> 00:13:30,643
No, I've got plans.

194
00:13:31,144 --> 00:13:33,813
I'll take you out
for something good next time. Go.

195
00:14:01,966 --> 00:14:03,718
-[car door opens]

196
00:14:43,549 --> 00:14:46,135
-[woman] Let me do it for you.
-[Minjae] No, I can do it quickly.

197
00:14:47,804 --> 00:14:50,473
[woman] I should've booked a table
in the hall, not a private room.

198
00:14:50,556 --> 00:14:52,391
[Minjae] No, the private room's good.
It's quiet.

199
00:14:54,310 --> 00:14:56,229
[woman] I didn't know
you wore sneakers like those.

200
00:14:56,729 --> 00:14:58,689
[Minjae] Yeah, why not? They're cute.

201
00:15:00,149 --> 00:15:03,986
[woman] Yeah. I guess you're still
young enough to pull these off. [chuckles]

202
00:15:12,411 --> 00:15:14,789
Try the seaweed soup with sea urchin.

203
00:15:14,872 --> 00:15:16,415
I ordered it in advance.

204
00:15:16,499 --> 00:15:17,500
[Minjae] Okay.

205
00:15:21,671 --> 00:15:22,880
Mmm...

206
00:15:22,964 --> 00:15:23,965
It's nice.

207
00:15:24,048 --> 00:15:27,927
You didn't even get to have seaweed soup
on your birthday, did you?

208
00:15:28,010 --> 00:15:31,055
Actually, I did.
I had seaweed soup and cake too.

209
00:15:32,640 --> 00:15:34,433
I did the whole birthday thing.

210
00:15:34,517 --> 00:15:36,310
And? What else did you do?

211
00:15:37,353 --> 00:15:39,772
[Minjae] And I went to the amusement park.

212
00:15:40,273 --> 00:15:42,441
I had a good time with friends.

213
00:15:43,985 --> 00:15:45,319
[woman] Okay, that's good.

214
00:15:45,403 --> 00:15:48,364
I wasn't able to do anything
for your birthday.

215
00:15:48,906 --> 00:15:50,908
[Minjae] Come on,
you're doing this for me now.

216
00:15:52,034 --> 00:15:55,413
Ah, right, you said Juwon's
in second grade now?

217
00:15:55,496 --> 00:15:57,707
Yeah, he's in second grade now.

218
00:15:57,790 --> 00:16:00,668
He'll be a senior next year,
but he just won't study. [chuckles]

219
00:16:00,751 --> 00:16:04,630
[chuckles] Just leave him alone.
He'll figure it out on his own.

220
00:16:05,256 --> 00:16:07,216
I was dead last in my class
at his age, too.

221
00:16:07,967 --> 00:16:10,845
You just didn't study
because you were busy training.

222
00:16:12,346 --> 00:16:14,807
You're incredibly smart.

223
00:16:17,101 --> 00:16:18,769
He's not like you.

224
00:16:18,853 --> 00:16:22,106
I think he takes after his dad.
He's not that smart. [chuckles]

225
00:16:22,190 --> 00:16:23,191
Ah...

226
00:16:24,275 --> 00:16:28,070
How's your husband doing? Busy as always?

227
00:16:28,154 --> 00:16:33,367
Mmm... Yeah. Well, he wanted to join us
today, but he just couldn't make the time.

228
00:16:34,368 --> 00:16:38,080
It's okay, there's always next time.
I know he's busy.

229
00:16:39,624 --> 00:16:40,625
Mmm...

230
00:16:41,334 --> 00:16:42,418
And this...

231
00:16:45,546 --> 00:16:47,048
Here. It's for your birthday.

232
00:16:48,507 --> 00:16:52,470
Just the dinner would've been enough.
You didn't have to buy anything.

233
00:16:52,970 --> 00:16:55,348
It's a watch. Open it.

234
00:16:55,431 --> 00:16:56,432
A watch?

235
00:17:00,937 --> 00:17:02,063
It's an expensive one.

236
00:17:03,439 --> 00:17:04,440
[woman] Do you like it?

237
00:17:06,275 --> 00:17:08,694
No, Mom, it's too expensive.

238
00:17:11,072 --> 00:17:12,531
Do you want me to put it on you?

239
00:17:13,115 --> 00:17:14,116
It's okay.

240
00:17:20,081 --> 00:17:21,749
Your clothes don't have to be fancy,

241
00:17:21,832 --> 00:17:24,460
but you should always
have on a nice watch and nice shoes.

242
00:17:29,507 --> 00:17:33,469
By the way, did your girlfriend
buy you those sneakers?

243
00:17:34,762 --> 00:17:36,514
No, I said I bought them.

244
00:17:36,597 --> 00:17:39,684
It's okay, you can tell me.
Are you being shy?

245
00:17:39,767 --> 00:17:42,436
No, I'm not being shy.
I really bought them myself.

246
00:17:44,730 --> 00:17:47,233
Fine. You don't need to tell me
if you don't want to.

247
00:17:48,192 --> 00:17:49,860
I'm being so nosy, aren't I?

248
00:17:55,533 --> 00:17:59,453
[sighs] Everyone says
you're nice and mature,

249
00:18:01,664 --> 00:18:03,791
but you're actually
narrow-minded and stubborn.

250
00:18:06,544 --> 00:18:07,962
That happened ages ago.

251
00:18:08,629 --> 00:18:10,798
Now, you're a grown man
well into your thirties,

252
00:18:10,881 --> 00:18:12,341
and you're still so immature.

253
00:18:13,509 --> 00:18:15,428
I know you're still holding it against me.

254
00:18:20,933 --> 00:18:22,643
What was I supposed to do,

255
00:18:23,227 --> 00:18:25,313
just let you die
when surgery could save you?

256
00:18:31,736 --> 00:18:35,364
You still should've asked me.

257
00:18:36,574 --> 00:18:39,619
What difference would it have made
if I'd asked you?

258
00:18:40,828 --> 00:18:42,663
There was no other choice.

259
00:18:43,247 --> 00:18:44,874
There were other options,

260
00:18:46,083 --> 00:18:48,044
and I should've been the one to decide.

261
00:18:52,840 --> 00:18:54,175
[sighs] Fine.

262
00:18:54,258 --> 00:18:58,095
I'm sick of having the same conversation.

263
00:19:03,059 --> 00:19:04,644
No matter how old you get,

264
00:19:05,353 --> 00:19:07,271
you'll never understand
how a parent feels.

265
00:19:07,855 --> 00:19:10,316
How... [chuckling] How a parent feels?

266
00:19:13,361 --> 00:19:14,987
Sorry, that was just too funny.

267
00:19:15,988 --> 00:19:16,989
Sorry.

268
00:19:21,994 --> 00:19:23,829
So why did you reach out to me then?

269
00:19:25,998 --> 00:19:27,208
Because I was young.

270
00:19:28,376 --> 00:19:30,044
I was told I was dying of cancer,

271
00:19:31,295 --> 00:19:33,798
so I wanted to see my birth mother
at least once.

272
00:19:35,299 --> 00:19:36,550
That's why I reached out.

273
00:19:39,178 --> 00:19:42,932
But still, you should've
just said hello and left.

274
00:19:43,933 --> 00:19:45,434
Why did you overstep?

275
00:19:50,898 --> 00:19:54,694
Today, I really braced myself
before coming here.

276
00:19:55,986 --> 00:19:57,697
But I just can never win with you.

277
00:21:36,420 --> 00:21:37,505
[angrily] For God's sake!

278
00:21:37,588 --> 00:21:39,381
What the hell is wrong with you?

279
00:21:39,465 --> 00:21:41,634
[yelling] Seriously,
what the hell is wrong with you?

280
00:21:41,717 --> 00:21:43,302
[muttering] What a freaking psycho.

281
00:21:43,385 --> 00:21:44,845
You piece of shit.

282
00:21:46,430 --> 00:21:47,640
[yells] God damn it!

283
00:22:09,286 --> 00:22:10,287
[Chansoo] <i>Was she pretty?</i>

284
00:22:10,371 --> 00:22:11,372
Was she?

285
00:22:12,414 --> 00:22:14,208
I only saw her back. Not her face.

286
00:22:14,291 --> 00:22:16,252
Come on, you should've seen her face.

287
00:22:16,794 --> 00:22:21,715
I didn't see her face,
but from behind, she had curly hair

288
00:22:21,799 --> 00:22:25,010
and this really polished,
expensive-looking vibe.

289
00:22:25,094 --> 00:22:26,470
Definitely not a Hongdae vibe.

290
00:22:27,847 --> 00:22:30,015
More like Gangnam, maybe?

291
00:22:30,099 --> 00:22:31,809
In other words, a pretty vibe?

292
00:22:31,892 --> 00:22:33,060
-[Sejin] Yes.
-Nice.

293
00:22:34,311 --> 00:22:39,108
But she had this mature vibe.

294
00:22:39,984 --> 00:22:43,070
She had this mature, older sister vibe.
That's the impression I got.

295
00:22:43,654 --> 00:22:45,656
Wait, could they be related then?

296
00:22:46,323 --> 00:22:48,617
Maybe she's his cousin or something.

297
00:22:49,326 --> 00:22:51,078
She's definitely not his cousin.

298
00:22:51,161 --> 00:22:53,914
She was touching his face like this.

299
00:22:56,250 --> 00:22:57,710
Let me call her.

300
00:22:57,793 --> 00:23:00,045
-[Sejin] Her? Who?
-Chacha.

301
00:23:05,301 --> 00:23:07,553
[hesitating] Hello, Seohyun.
You picked up fast.

302
00:23:07,636 --> 00:23:11,140
Are you busy? Okay, you're busy,
but let me ask you something real quick.

303
00:23:11,223 --> 00:23:16,145
Apparently, someone saw Minjae secretly
meeting up with some woman. Mmm...

304
00:23:16,228 --> 00:23:20,149
She was squeezing his cheeks like this.

305
00:23:20,232 --> 00:23:23,319
Then they got into a white Mercedes
and drove off together.

306
00:23:23,402 --> 00:23:24,403
Yes.

307
00:23:24,486 --> 00:23:26,822
Yeah, right. Yeah.

308
00:23:28,157 --> 00:23:29,366
What?

309
00:23:29,450 --> 00:23:30,451
Yeah.

310
00:23:30,534 --> 00:23:32,494
What does she say? Does she know her?

311
00:23:33,162 --> 00:23:34,747
[Taeho] No, wait.

312
00:23:34,830 --> 00:23:36,165
[whispering] She says it's not like

313
00:23:36,248 --> 00:23:38,167
there's only one white Mercedes
in the world.

314
00:23:38,250 --> 00:23:40,419
She's right.
Hey, did you see the license plate?

315
00:23:40,502 --> 00:23:43,172
-No, I didn't.
-[mumbles] You should've seen that.

316
00:23:43,255 --> 00:23:44,757
[in normal voice] Hello? Seohyun, yes.

317
00:23:44,840 --> 00:23:47,009
No, we don't know
the license plate number.

318
00:23:48,636 --> 00:23:51,764
No, Seohyun,
I don't think that's necessary. Yeah.

319
00:23:52,890 --> 00:23:54,683
No. Wait, no.

320
00:23:54,767 --> 00:23:57,311
-No, that's... No. What the hell?
-[line disconnects]

321
00:23:57,937 --> 00:23:59,897
What is it? Why?

322
00:23:59,980 --> 00:24:02,274
Damn it. She's coming to school again.

323
00:24:02,358 --> 00:24:03,359
Why?

324
00:24:03,442 --> 00:24:06,278
-From now on, don't call Seohyun.
-Yeah.

325
00:24:06,362 --> 00:24:08,739
-We can handle things on our own.
-Okay.

326
00:24:09,823 --> 00:24:12,034
Seriously, what is wrong with you? [tuts]

327
00:24:14,954 --> 00:24:16,872
Handle? Handle what?

328
00:24:17,498 --> 00:24:18,666
[Chansoo] Huh?

329
00:24:18,749 --> 00:24:20,459
What did you guys do this time?

330
00:24:20,542 --> 00:24:21,543
[Taeho] Minjae.

331
00:24:21,627 --> 00:24:22,628
[Minjae] Yeah?

332
00:24:23,128 --> 00:24:24,964
[Taeho] Even Seohyun said she didn't know.

333
00:24:25,047 --> 00:24:26,048
Who was she?

334
00:24:27,257 --> 00:24:29,718
Hey, you even called Seohyun?

335
00:24:29,802 --> 00:24:34,515
Apparently, she was smiling
and squishing your face like this.

336
00:24:34,598 --> 00:24:36,433
And you had a big smile on your face.

337
00:24:36,517 --> 00:24:39,645
I had a big smile? Me?

338
00:24:40,145 --> 00:24:41,438
-Well...
-[Minjae] When?

339
00:24:41,522 --> 00:24:43,857
That's what I heard. [chuckles]

340
00:24:43,941 --> 00:24:45,651
There's a witness, you know.

341
00:24:45,734 --> 00:24:48,070
Who's that crazy witness? Tell me. Huh?

342
00:24:49,029 --> 00:24:52,533
She's not your cousin, is she?

343
00:24:52,616 --> 00:24:55,953
No, she's not a relative
or anyone from his family.

344
00:24:56,036 --> 00:24:57,871
Why would his cousin touch his face?

345
00:24:58,455 --> 00:25:00,290
Even siblings don't do that.

346
00:25:05,546 --> 00:25:08,257
Right. She's not my cousin.

347
00:25:13,345 --> 00:25:14,972
She's someone I used to like.

348
00:25:16,765 --> 00:25:18,475
I still like her.

349
00:25:19,810 --> 00:25:23,022
So are you two dating or something?

350
00:25:23,105 --> 00:25:25,107
No, we're not dating.

351
00:25:25,190 --> 00:25:26,316
She's married.

352
00:25:26,400 --> 00:25:27,901
She has a son too.

353
00:25:28,736 --> 00:25:29,737
Uh...

354
00:25:30,404 --> 00:25:33,490
Wait, you met up
with a married woman? Why?

355
00:25:34,491 --> 00:25:37,870
Well, she said she wanted to see me
for my birthday, so I met up with her.

356
00:25:38,454 --> 00:25:41,373
She even got me an expensive watch
for my birthday.

357
00:25:41,457 --> 00:25:42,708
I'll wear it next time.

358
00:25:44,710 --> 00:25:46,420
Anyone else have any questions?

359
00:25:46,503 --> 00:25:48,505
Minjae, does that mean you've been...

360
00:25:48,589 --> 00:25:49,882
[Youjin] But she's married.

361
00:25:50,466 --> 00:25:53,677
Meeting up because she missed you
and exchanging gifts? That's just weird.

362
00:25:53,761 --> 00:25:55,471
We're kind of weird.

363
00:25:56,055 --> 00:25:58,891
"We..." [scoffs] "We"?

364
00:25:58,974 --> 00:26:00,434
Yes, we. She and I.

365
00:26:04,772 --> 00:26:08,567
If you're still so hung up on each other,
why don't you get back together?

366
00:26:08,650 --> 00:26:09,777
She can get divorced.

367
00:26:09,860 --> 00:26:12,237
Come on, realistically,
divorce would be a bit much.

368
00:26:12,738 --> 00:26:13,947
[Youjin] No, it's not.

369
00:26:14,031 --> 00:26:16,116
They say love transcends borders and age.

370
00:26:17,076 --> 00:26:18,952
She should get divorced first, okay?

371
00:26:19,036 --> 00:26:21,663
Don't sneak around,
deceiving and betraying people.

372
00:26:21,747 --> 00:26:23,248
Wait, what are you talking about?

373
00:26:23,332 --> 00:26:25,918
When did I ever deceive or betray anyone?

374
00:26:27,961 --> 00:26:29,379
You're deceiving her husband.

375
00:26:29,463 --> 00:26:30,464
[Minjae] No.

376
00:26:31,173 --> 00:26:33,967
He knows everything.
Her husband and I know each other.

377
00:26:35,427 --> 00:26:36,804
-[Youjin] Her husband knows?
-[Minjae] Yes.

378
00:26:38,222 --> 00:26:40,015
[scoffs] You people are so weird.

379
00:26:40,099 --> 00:26:41,475
I told you we're weird.

380
00:26:43,977 --> 00:26:45,479
Anything else you want to know?

381
00:26:45,562 --> 00:26:47,106
-Chansoo, how about you?
-Minjae.

382
00:26:47,189 --> 00:26:48,398
So if she asks to see you again...

383
00:26:48,482 --> 00:26:49,483
[Minjae] Uh, yes?

384
00:26:50,609 --> 00:26:51,860
...are you going to?

385
00:26:54,071 --> 00:26:56,573
Yeah, if she wants to see me,
I'll see her.

386
00:27:10,295 --> 00:27:11,547
Thank you.

387
00:27:11,630 --> 00:27:12,631
[Chansoo] Are you okay?

388
00:27:13,423 --> 00:27:14,424
[Youjin] Yes.

389
00:27:18,720 --> 00:27:21,223
[Sejin whispering] It's nothing.
It's just that time of the month.

390
00:27:21,306 --> 00:27:23,058
You know, girl stuff.

391
00:27:24,810 --> 00:27:25,811
What?

392
00:27:25,894 --> 00:27:27,855
[Youjin] I just don't understand.

393
00:27:29,106 --> 00:27:30,357
I'm talking about Minjae.

394
00:27:31,400 --> 00:27:33,193
What on earth goes on in men's heads...

395
00:27:37,239 --> 00:27:38,740
No, never mind.

396
00:27:38,824 --> 00:27:42,035
[Chansoo] Taeho, is Seohyun...
I mean, did you tell her not to come?

397
00:27:42,119 --> 00:27:44,079
She's not coming. [chuckles] Don't worry.

398
00:27:44,621 --> 00:27:47,749
Damn, we almost had that crazy girl
show up again. [chuckles]

399
00:27:47,833 --> 00:27:49,626
Hey, you think this is funny?

400
00:27:51,003 --> 00:27:52,004
Right. [sighs]

401
00:27:52,504 --> 00:27:54,840
Shouldn't we do something about it?

402
00:27:56,091 --> 00:27:59,261
I mean, no matter how much he likes her,
she's married.

403
00:28:00,429 --> 00:28:02,890
It's just morally and ethically wrong.

404
00:28:02,973 --> 00:28:04,099
Just leave him be.

405
00:28:04,641 --> 00:28:06,810
They like each other.
It's none of our business.

406
00:28:07,769 --> 00:28:10,480
Just leave him be.
Let him live, die, or stay like garbage.

407
00:28:10,564 --> 00:28:11,899
Let him do whatever he wants.

408
00:28:12,482 --> 00:28:16,862
But still,
we can't just sit back and watch.

409
00:28:16,945 --> 00:28:19,781
Yeah. Then the crazy girl
will show up again.

410
00:28:20,949 --> 00:28:23,076
So, do you have any idea
what we should do?

411
00:28:23,160 --> 00:28:25,537
[inhales sharply] Let's see.

412
00:28:26,163 --> 00:28:28,081
You said she was really pretty, right?

413
00:28:35,047 --> 00:28:37,674
We can find a prettier woman
and set him up with her.

414
00:28:38,634 --> 00:28:40,302
-[Hangyeol and Chansoo] Oh!
-[Taeho] Yeah.

415
00:28:40,802 --> 00:28:41,970
Right, Youjin.

416
00:28:42,054 --> 00:28:46,266
Do you have any pretty friends
we could set him up with?

417
00:28:46,934 --> 00:28:47,935
No.

418
00:28:48,518 --> 00:28:51,355
He's petty and weird.
Whoever we set him up with would hate us.

419
00:28:51,438 --> 00:28:52,439
[Taeho mumbles] True.

420
00:28:55,734 --> 00:28:57,653
We'd have to mention his disability, too.

421
00:28:57,736 --> 00:29:00,155
It wouldn't be easy
to set him up with normal people.

422
00:29:01,657 --> 00:29:02,658
[Youjin] Hey, you.

423
00:29:03,158 --> 00:29:04,159
"Hey, you?"

424
00:29:04,743 --> 00:29:06,995
We're the same age,
so I'll drop the formalities.

425
00:29:07,079 --> 00:29:08,664
What exactly did you mean by that?

426
00:29:08,747 --> 00:29:10,040
What?

427
00:29:10,123 --> 00:29:12,626
You said there are normal people,
and Minjae is disabled.

428
00:29:12,709 --> 00:29:15,295
Are you saying he's abnormal
or somehow less of a person?

429
00:29:16,672 --> 00:29:17,673
No.

430
00:29:17,756 --> 00:29:20,258
What do you mean, no?
That's exactly what you said.

431
00:29:20,342 --> 00:29:23,136
Why are you talking so disrespectfully
about your senior?

432
00:29:23,220 --> 00:29:26,181
You also just called him petty and weird

433
00:29:26,264 --> 00:29:28,475
and said anyone we set him up with
would hate us.

434
00:29:29,267 --> 00:29:32,020
[scoffs] What I said is different
from what you said.

435
00:29:32,104 --> 00:29:33,981
Different? Different how?

436
00:29:38,151 --> 00:29:40,862
What? A blind date, all of a sudden?

437
00:29:40,946 --> 00:29:43,907
[Youjin] <i>Yeah.</i>
<i>You saw him the other day too.</i>

438
00:29:43,991 --> 00:29:45,575
Park Minjae, our lab lead.

439
00:29:47,244 --> 00:29:51,289
He's really cool, good-looking, and kind.

440
00:29:51,373 --> 00:29:53,375
And he's smart too.

441
00:29:53,458 --> 00:29:56,461
That senior from your lab
who works as a research assistant?

442
00:29:57,879 --> 00:29:59,631
Yeah, of course I remember him.

443
00:30:00,424 --> 00:30:02,342
But a blind date with him?

444
00:30:04,011 --> 00:30:05,012
Yeah.

445
00:30:06,430 --> 00:30:07,597
It's not that.

446
00:30:08,432 --> 00:30:11,268
I'm just too busy right now
to think about anything else.

447
00:30:11,768 --> 00:30:13,979
[Youjin] <i>Oh... Yeah, of course.</i>

448
00:30:15,272 --> 00:30:17,065
Well, if you're busy, that's okay.

449
00:30:17,149 --> 00:30:18,191
All right.

450
00:30:18,817 --> 00:30:19,818
Bye.

451
00:30:22,154 --> 00:30:24,239
[sighs] She's too busy.

452
00:30:37,794 --> 00:30:41,006
[Subin] Professor, here's the research
I did on the papers you mentioned.

453
00:30:41,089 --> 00:30:42,674
Okay. Thank you.

454
00:30:44,009 --> 00:30:47,262
Was the call you just got about someone
setting you up on a blind date?

455
00:30:47,929 --> 00:30:49,848
[Subin chuckling] Uh, yes.

456
00:30:50,682 --> 00:30:53,477
Work is important,
but you need to put yourself out there

457
00:30:53,560 --> 00:30:56,063
and date while you're young and pretty.

458
00:30:57,064 --> 00:30:59,066
Look at me. Time flies.

459
00:30:59,149 --> 00:31:02,152
Mmm... You're still young and pretty.

460
00:31:02,235 --> 00:31:04,112
Are you teasing me right now?

461
00:31:04,696 --> 00:31:05,697
Enough already.

462
00:31:07,783 --> 00:31:09,451
That was Youjin on the phone, right?

463
00:31:10,368 --> 00:31:11,369
[Subin] Yes.

464
00:31:11,870 --> 00:31:15,123
Was she trying to set you up
with that disabled guy?

465
00:31:15,207 --> 00:31:16,208
Uh...

466
00:31:17,626 --> 00:31:20,003
If he's so great,
why doesn't she date him herself?

467
00:31:20,087 --> 00:31:22,297
You don't set a friend up
with someone like that.

468
00:31:23,006 --> 00:31:26,635
I don't think that's...
He seemed like a nice person, though.

469
00:31:27,135 --> 00:31:30,347
Youjin must think so too.
That's why she tried to set me up with...

470
00:31:31,681 --> 00:31:34,851
Did she really not know he was disabled
before you mentioned it?

471
00:31:35,936 --> 00:31:37,938
Yeah, it looked like she had no idea.

472
00:31:38,021 --> 00:31:39,648
She seemed really surprised.

473
00:31:39,731 --> 00:31:41,733
You didn't say
you heard it from me, did you?

474
00:31:42,359 --> 00:31:44,152
[Subin] I didn't say that.

475
00:31:45,403 --> 00:31:49,783
Well, once something catches my interest,
I can't help wanting to know more.

476
00:31:50,867 --> 00:31:54,287
[sighs] My memory is just too good
for my own good.

477
00:31:55,247 --> 00:31:56,998
It's exhausting, but what can I do?

478
00:31:57,082 --> 00:32:00,377
I never forget
and always return even the smallest favor.

479
00:32:03,380 --> 00:32:04,381
You can go now.

480
00:32:04,923 --> 00:32:05,924
Okay.

481
00:32:12,806 --> 00:32:15,642
I mean, it never made sense
from the start.

482
00:32:16,351 --> 00:32:20,021
He's already into someone,
and we set him up with another woman?

483
00:32:20,105 --> 00:32:21,356
That's just ridiculous.

484
00:32:21,439 --> 00:32:23,525
[Taeho] Well, Youjin, you're saying that

485
00:32:23,608 --> 00:32:26,736
because you're still young
and don't understand men yet.

486
00:32:26,820 --> 00:32:28,113
Men aren't like that.

487
00:32:28,780 --> 00:32:31,241
We believe we can find love anytime,

488
00:32:31,324 --> 00:32:33,160
so we always keep our options open.

489
00:32:33,910 --> 00:32:36,079
Yeah, there's even a song

490
00:32:36,163 --> 00:32:38,373
called "A Love Is Forgotten
by Another Love."

491
00:32:47,424 --> 00:32:49,426
-Such a great song.
-[Taeho] It sure is.

492
00:32:49,926 --> 00:32:55,432
But Minjae isn't the type of guy who jumps
from one woman to another, is he?

493
00:32:56,057 --> 00:33:00,187
Youjin, all men are basically the same.

494
00:33:00,770 --> 00:33:02,063
We're all the same.

495
00:33:03,565 --> 00:33:06,860
But I understand why Youjin is concerned.

496
00:33:07,736 --> 00:33:09,988
No, I'm not. I'm not concerned.

497
00:33:10,906 --> 00:33:14,117
Minjae doesn't do blind dates,
so he might say no.

498
00:33:15,493 --> 00:33:17,579
[Youjin] Yeah, exactly.
That's what I'm talking about.

499
00:33:18,496 --> 00:33:19,748
[Hangyeol] He might.

500
00:33:20,248 --> 00:33:22,876
Shy people
can find blind dates uncomfortable.

501
00:33:22,959 --> 00:33:26,671
The bottom line is,
it doesn't have to be a blind date.

502
00:33:26,755 --> 00:33:28,673
But it has to feel like fate.

503
00:33:28,757 --> 00:33:31,760
Yeah. Like getting hit by a bike,

504
00:33:31,843 --> 00:33:35,388
dropping a handkerchief,
or accidentally swapping phones.

505
00:33:35,472 --> 00:33:37,557
You know, stuff we see in movies
all the time.

506
00:33:37,641 --> 00:33:40,852
We can work out the details later.

507
00:33:40,936 --> 00:33:41,937
The problem is...

508
00:33:42,687 --> 00:33:44,773
we haven't found a woman for him yet.

509
00:33:48,985 --> 00:33:53,531
Hey, Lim Youjin. Try calling someone else.
Don't you have any other friends?

510
00:33:53,615 --> 00:33:55,242
-I don't.
-[cellphone vibrates]

511
00:33:55,325 --> 00:33:57,619
Guys, don't worry. Yeah, we got the woman.

512
00:33:57,702 --> 00:33:58,703
[Chansoo] What?

513
00:33:58,787 --> 00:34:00,705
Seohyun has someone from work.

514
00:34:00,789 --> 00:34:01,998
What?

515
00:34:02,082 --> 00:34:04,501
[Taeho] Wow, she's really pretty.

516
00:34:04,584 --> 00:34:06,586
-Guys, have a look.
-[Hangyeol] Sorry, Youjin.

517
00:34:18,556 --> 00:34:20,558
-[Hangyeol] I think she looks nice.
-[men exclaiming]

518
00:34:40,161 --> 00:34:41,746
LIM YOUJIN

519
00:34:41,830 --> 00:34:42,956
[Youjin] <i>What are you up to?</i>

520
00:34:48,003 --> 00:34:49,421
[Minjae] <i>I'm on my way somewhere.</i>

521
00:34:53,341 --> 00:34:54,509
[Youjin] <i>To the movies?</i>

522
00:34:56,177 --> 00:34:57,178
<i>With Seohyun?</i>

523
00:35:02,642 --> 00:35:03,810
[Minjae] <i>How did you know?</i>

524
00:35:05,103 --> 00:35:06,938
<i>What movie are you going to watch?</i>

525
00:35:08,648 --> 00:35:09,774
[Minjae] <i>Not going to tell you.</i>

526
00:35:16,239 --> 00:35:17,907
[Youjin] <i>Can I join you?</i>

527
00:35:23,121 --> 00:35:25,290
[Minjae] <i>Yeah, no, get lost.</i>

528
00:36:15,215 --> 00:36:16,216
Hello?

529
00:36:18,885 --> 00:36:19,886
Hello?

530
00:36:21,763 --> 00:36:22,764
Hel--

531
00:36:34,484 --> 00:36:35,860
[Youjin] I won't keep you long.

532
00:36:38,905 --> 00:36:41,533
Okay. What is it you wanted to say?

533
00:36:51,209 --> 00:36:52,919
I know you're mad at me.

534
00:36:55,547 --> 00:36:57,132
We're talking about this again?

535
00:36:58,174 --> 00:37:01,094
Look, I apologized.
What more do you want me to do?

536
00:37:01,177 --> 00:37:02,429
That's not what happened.

537
00:37:03,638 --> 00:37:07,308
I apologized to you,
but you got mad and were being sarcastic.

538
00:37:11,104 --> 00:37:12,689
I know what I did wasn't right.

539
00:37:14,399 --> 00:37:16,276
So you could've just yelled at me,

540
00:37:17,318 --> 00:37:20,238
or told me to keep apologizing
until you felt better.

541
00:37:22,574 --> 00:37:24,409
Why get all sarcastic and mean?

542
00:37:25,410 --> 00:37:26,578
Okay, sorry.

543
00:37:27,328 --> 00:37:29,330
I didn't mean to be sarcastic, though.

544
00:37:31,124 --> 00:37:33,793
I don't know.
I think that's just how I am. I'm sorry.

545
00:37:34,794 --> 00:37:35,837
Again...

546
00:37:35,920 --> 00:37:37,046
Shall we head out now?

547
00:37:37,839 --> 00:37:38,840
[Youjin] But...

548
00:37:41,426 --> 00:37:43,303
No matter how petty and mean you get,

549
00:37:44,763 --> 00:37:46,389
I just can't seem to hate you.

550
00:37:49,559 --> 00:37:53,062
I get annoyed, I get angry,
and I don't understand you,

551
00:37:55,148 --> 00:37:56,733
but I just can't seem to hate you.

552
00:37:58,777 --> 00:38:00,278
Actually, it's more than that.

553
00:38:03,656 --> 00:38:04,699
I just...

554
00:38:06,284 --> 00:38:07,577
keep wanting to see you.

555
00:38:12,248 --> 00:38:13,708
I want to see you,

556
00:38:15,084 --> 00:38:16,461
and I want to be with you.

557
00:38:19,589 --> 00:38:21,674
I don't want to lose you to someone else.

558
00:38:22,675 --> 00:38:25,386
I don't know how to put it, but...

559
00:38:32,227 --> 00:38:33,228
I...

560
00:38:34,813 --> 00:38:35,939
like you.

561
00:38:37,607 --> 00:38:39,317
I like you a lot.

562
00:39:02,882 --> 00:39:05,677
I know I'm the woman here,
but I'm going to put my pride aside

563
00:39:07,303 --> 00:39:08,721
and make the first move.

564
00:39:11,641 --> 00:39:12,767
Park Minjae...

565
00:39:15,186 --> 00:39:16,312
I like you.

566
00:39:18,231 --> 00:39:20,066
I want you to be my boyfriend.

567
00:39:39,752 --> 00:39:41,045
Wow.

568
00:39:44,173 --> 00:39:45,550
You're really...

569
00:39:49,137 --> 00:39:51,806
Did you really not see it,
or are you just pretending?

570
00:39:52,891 --> 00:39:53,892
[Youjin] What?

571
00:39:57,353 --> 00:40:00,356
I mean, I'm not trying
to be sarcastic or mean here.

572
00:40:02,233 --> 00:40:03,443
You know what?

573
00:40:03,526 --> 00:40:07,030
I'm going to put my pride as a man aside
and be honest with you.

574
00:40:09,073 --> 00:40:10,074
Imagine...

575
00:40:11,659 --> 00:40:13,036
how I felt...

576
00:40:14,996 --> 00:40:16,581
after you left like that.

577
00:40:19,083 --> 00:40:22,712
Of course, I know you were
caught off guard and scared too.

578
00:40:23,671 --> 00:40:24,672
I...

579
00:40:24,756 --> 00:40:26,716
[Minjae] What about me?
How do you think I felt?

580
00:40:27,383 --> 00:40:31,220
How do you think I felt
after you just left like that?

581
00:40:34,098 --> 00:40:35,850
Can you imagine how I must've felt?

582
00:40:40,021 --> 00:40:41,481
My heart broke.

583
00:40:42,815 --> 00:40:44,150
I wanted to die.

584
00:40:49,364 --> 00:40:50,365
I'm...

585
00:40:51,991 --> 00:40:54,953
shy, I'm a coward,

586
00:40:56,663 --> 00:40:58,039
and I've been hurt before.

587
00:41:01,250 --> 00:41:03,169
I'm not the right person for you.

588
00:41:09,300 --> 00:41:10,635
I'm officially...

589
00:41:13,012 --> 00:41:14,514
turning you down.

590
00:41:18,017 --> 00:41:22,605
I hope this doesn't make things awkward
between us in the lab.

591
00:41:26,401 --> 00:41:27,527
I'm going to head out.

592
00:43:08,294 --> 00:43:09,295
[Minjae mumbles] You scared me.

593
00:44:49,645 --> 00:44:52,273
[groans] I've been washing it with soap,

594
00:44:52,356 --> 00:44:53,983
but the grease just won't come out.

595
00:44:54,609 --> 00:44:57,028
So just put on the gloves like me.

596
00:44:57,111 --> 00:44:58,946
I mean, I don't even like dumplings.

597
00:44:59,030 --> 00:45:01,324
And Lim Youjin is going to eat
all of those anyway.

598
00:45:02,074 --> 00:45:03,910
Honestly, I hope she does.

599
00:45:04,535 --> 00:45:07,205
She's eating like a bird these days.

600
00:45:07,288 --> 00:45:10,041
I bet she's eating plenty of good food
when she's out.

601
00:45:11,125 --> 00:45:13,294
Call Youjin and tell her
I'm making dumplings,

602
00:45:13,377 --> 00:45:14,837
so she should come home early.

603
00:45:26,641 --> 00:45:27,808
Hello?

604
00:45:27,892 --> 00:45:30,144
[Youseong] <i>Hey, Lim Youjin.</i>
<i>Where are you now?</i>

605
00:45:31,312 --> 00:45:34,398
I'm at school. Where else would I be?
I said I was going to school.

606
00:45:34,899 --> 00:45:38,361
I'd bet my last penny
you're out having fun, not at school.

607
00:45:40,863 --> 00:45:43,824
Hey, where are you?
I'm making dumplings now.

608
00:45:46,369 --> 00:45:47,453
Yeah.

609
00:45:48,621 --> 00:45:49,664
Okay.

610
00:45:49,747 --> 00:45:51,832
All right. Don't be late.

611
00:45:51,916 --> 00:45:52,917
Okay.

612
00:45:53,000 --> 00:45:54,460
-You can hang up now.
-Hey, you--

613
00:45:55,628 --> 00:45:56,963
When is she going to be home?

614
00:45:57,046 --> 00:45:58,881
She's going to study before coming home.

615
00:45:58,965 --> 00:46:01,592
But she'll be back for dinner
and have the dumplings.

616
00:46:02,426 --> 00:46:05,221
She's not at school right now.
She's out somewhere with a man.

617
00:46:06,889 --> 00:46:09,517
Fine. Good luck betting
what little money you have on it.

618
00:46:09,600 --> 00:46:11,143
I have proof.

619
00:46:11,727 --> 00:46:14,981
-What proof?
-Proof that Lim Youjin is seeing a guy.

620
00:46:16,732 --> 00:46:18,859
Did you read Youjin's diary again?

621
00:46:18,943 --> 00:46:20,945
Come on, I told you to stop doing that.

622
00:46:21,529 --> 00:46:23,906
I only did that
until she was in high school.

623
00:46:23,990 --> 00:46:26,325
That brat stopped
keeping a diary in college.

624
00:46:28,411 --> 00:46:30,538
So if it's not her diary,
what's the proof?

625
00:46:31,038 --> 00:46:33,624
You want to know?
Then give me 100,000 won.

626
00:46:36,085 --> 00:46:38,337
What? 100,000 won isn't much.

627
00:46:38,421 --> 00:46:40,214
You keep that proof to yourself.

628
00:46:41,173 --> 00:46:44,093
Or you and Youjin
will be at each other's throats again.

629
00:46:44,593 --> 00:46:47,263
And Mom will kick your ass again.

630
00:46:47,346 --> 00:46:48,347
Fine.

631
00:46:49,307 --> 00:46:52,143
If you don't want to know, forget it.
It's no loss to me.

632
00:46:54,395 --> 00:46:56,105
Do you really have proof?

633
00:46:56,188 --> 00:46:58,858
Yes, I have solid evidence.

634
00:47:00,901 --> 00:47:03,612
All right. I'll give you 100,000 won.
Bring it here.

635
00:47:03,696 --> 00:47:07,199
Really? Really? You promise? 100,000 won.

636
00:47:07,283 --> 00:47:08,451
You're so dead now.

637
00:47:10,786 --> 00:47:13,080
Hey, don't go through Youjin's stuff.

638
00:47:16,334 --> 00:47:19,670
[Youseong] Where did it go?
It was right here.

639
00:47:21,505 --> 00:47:22,506
[Miyoung] Hey.

640
00:47:23,591 --> 00:47:24,592
[Youseong] Where is it?

641
00:47:26,010 --> 00:47:28,304
Hey, stop going through her stuff.

642
00:47:29,347 --> 00:47:30,765
Don't give him the money, okay?

643
00:47:31,557 --> 00:47:33,309
[chuckling] What?
I don't even have 10 won.

644
00:47:34,268 --> 00:47:35,353
[Youseong] Where did it go?

645
00:47:35,436 --> 00:47:37,772
[Miyoung] I told you to stop
snooping around in Youjin's room.

646
00:47:37,855 --> 00:47:39,815
But it was definitely there.

647
00:47:39,899 --> 00:47:41,567
Please. There's no proof.

648
00:47:42,651 --> 00:47:46,197
I knew this would happen,
so I made sure to gather more evidence.

649
00:47:46,280 --> 00:47:47,365
Just wait.

650
00:47:48,366 --> 00:47:50,701
Look. You still don't believe me?

651
00:47:50,785 --> 00:47:52,203
You still don't?

652
00:47:52,286 --> 00:47:53,287
[Miyoung] Oh my.

653
00:47:55,289 --> 00:47:56,665
Oh my gosh. Matching rings?

654
00:47:57,375 --> 00:47:59,794
I'm sure she's with her boyfriend
right now.

655
00:48:16,852 --> 00:48:19,397
OUT OF OFFICE

656
00:48:59,228 --> 00:49:00,688
[Jihoon] Are you feeling unwell?

657
00:49:00,771 --> 00:49:03,983
[Youjin weakly] No. I took some medicine,
so I should be fine soon.

658
00:49:05,067 --> 00:49:06,735
Thank you. You can go.

659
00:49:07,778 --> 00:49:09,697
Hold on to me and try to stand up.

660
00:49:10,656 --> 00:49:12,324
-[Youjin exclaims in pain]
-[Jihoon] Oh!

661
00:49:12,408 --> 00:49:13,868
-[Youjin moaning in pain]
-[Jihoon] I think you should see a doctor.

662
00:49:27,548 --> 00:49:29,967
We're almost at the hospital,
so hang in there.

663
00:49:30,759 --> 00:49:32,428
[Youjin groans softly] I'm okay.

664
00:49:33,137 --> 00:49:36,515
You can just drop me off at the bus stop.

665
00:49:37,391 --> 00:49:39,435
-[mumbles] No, you're not okay.
-[Youjin groans]

666
00:49:40,769 --> 00:49:44,356
[weakly] Are you Professor Talking Hat?

667
00:49:51,363 --> 00:49:53,282
Are you delirious from being sick?

668
00:49:53,365 --> 00:49:54,909
[chuckling] Yeah.

669
00:49:54,992 --> 00:49:57,286
I guess I am. [chuckles]

670
00:50:07,379 --> 00:50:08,547
[Jihoon] What? What did you say?

671
00:50:09,465 --> 00:50:11,759
[groans softly] Mom.

672
00:50:13,385 --> 00:50:14,803
Mom.

673
00:50:40,913 --> 00:50:42,873
[doctor] When you're ready.
One, two, three.

674
00:50:59,390 --> 00:51:01,976
INCORRECT PATTERN

675
00:51:02,685 --> 00:51:05,062
INCORRECT PATTERN

676
00:51:13,195 --> 00:51:14,280
[Jihoon] Hello.

677
00:51:14,363 --> 00:51:15,739
It is appendicitis.

678
00:51:15,823 --> 00:51:18,117
She needs emergency surgery immediately.

679
00:51:18,200 --> 00:51:19,201
Are you her family?

680
00:51:19,285 --> 00:51:22,037
No, I'm not her family.
She's a student at my university.

681
00:51:22,121 --> 00:51:23,497
[doctor] You're her teacher.

682
00:51:24,456 --> 00:51:27,001
It's urgent, so please sign here first.

683
00:51:29,587 --> 00:51:30,754
-Sign here?
-[doctor] Yes.

684
00:51:54,361 --> 00:51:57,865
INCOMING CALL
MOM

685
00:51:58,741 --> 00:52:00,993
Hello. This is Lim Youjin's phone.

686
00:52:12,421 --> 00:52:13,964
We're looking for Lim Youjin...

687
00:52:14,590 --> 00:52:16,675
[staff] She went into surgery
a little while ago.

688
00:52:16,759 --> 00:52:17,885
Right. Okay.

689
00:52:18,385 --> 00:52:19,845
Where's the operating room?

690
00:52:19,928 --> 00:52:21,847
-[staff] Just go one floor up.
-[Yongseok] Okay.

691
00:52:22,514 --> 00:52:23,515
[Miyoung] Thank you.

692
00:52:55,839 --> 00:52:56,840
[Youjin] Mmm...

693
00:53:03,389 --> 00:53:04,431
[Miyoung] Youjin.

694
00:53:06,350 --> 00:53:07,810
Youjin, are you okay?

695
00:53:07,893 --> 00:53:09,561
It's Mom.

696
00:53:09,645 --> 00:53:12,773
-[Youjin] Mom.
-Yeah. Dad's here too.

697
00:53:12,856 --> 00:53:13,857
Yeah.

698
00:53:14,650 --> 00:53:15,693
[Miyoung] Yeah.

699
00:53:16,777 --> 00:53:18,987
-[weakly] Mom. [sobs]
-[Miyoung] Yeah.

700
00:53:19,071 --> 00:53:20,155
Does it hurt?

701
00:53:21,115 --> 00:53:22,282
Does it hurt a lot?

702
00:53:23,158 --> 00:53:24,618
No, I'm okay.

703
00:53:26,620 --> 00:53:29,373
[mumbles] You did great. You did so well.

704
00:53:43,721 --> 00:53:44,722
Excuse me.

705
00:53:45,514 --> 00:53:46,849
It's past 9 a.m.

706
00:53:49,643 --> 00:53:52,855
It's past 9 a.m.,
and Lim Youjin is not here again.

707
00:53:56,108 --> 00:53:58,569
She's late again. [sighs]

708
00:54:00,696 --> 00:54:02,448
Should I give her a call?

709
00:54:08,162 --> 00:54:09,413
Should I give her a call?

710
00:54:09,496 --> 00:54:11,623
Just leave her alone.
She'll get here eventually.

711
00:54:17,212 --> 00:54:19,548
Hey, if you're late, just come.
Why are you calling...

712
00:54:21,884 --> 00:54:23,427
Yes, hello, ma'am.

713
00:54:23,510 --> 00:54:27,973
[sighing] Uh...
I should've called earlier.

714
00:54:28,056 --> 00:54:29,057
I'm so sorry.

715
00:54:29,141 --> 00:54:32,644
No, not at all.
I didn't know it was you, ma'am.

716
00:54:33,479 --> 00:54:34,897
I'm so sorry.

717
00:54:34,980 --> 00:54:36,231
Yes.

718
00:54:36,315 --> 00:54:37,316
No.

719
00:54:38,358 --> 00:54:39,359
Yes.

720
00:54:41,111 --> 00:54:42,446
Youjin?

721
00:54:43,363 --> 00:54:44,990
Oh... She's doing great.

722
00:54:45,073 --> 00:54:47,618
She works hard, she's talented,

723
00:54:47,701 --> 00:54:50,537
and the professors
all speak very highly of her.

724
00:54:50,621 --> 00:54:52,414
Is that her mom calling right now?

725
00:54:55,626 --> 00:54:56,627
Yes.

726
00:54:58,378 --> 00:54:59,379
Yes.

727
00:55:00,631 --> 00:55:02,883
Ah... I see.

728
00:55:03,967 --> 00:55:04,968
Yes.

729
00:55:06,261 --> 00:55:07,262
Okay.

730
00:55:08,555 --> 00:55:10,140
Yes, I understand.

731
00:55:11,183 --> 00:55:13,810
Please tell her she doesn't need
to worry about the lab

732
00:55:13,894 --> 00:55:15,729
and to just focus on getting better.

733
00:55:15,812 --> 00:55:19,775
[chuckling] Yes,
thank you so much for understanding.

734
00:55:20,400 --> 00:55:23,153
Okay, take care. Bye.

735
00:55:26,156 --> 00:55:27,866
-[line disconnects]
-[sighs in relief, chuckles softly]

736
00:55:28,951 --> 00:55:33,080
Hey, your senior's so polite,
and he has such a nice voice.

737
00:55:34,790 --> 00:55:35,791
No, he doesn't.

738
00:55:41,922 --> 00:55:44,383
She had her mom call?
Is she in elementary school?

739
00:55:44,466 --> 00:55:45,759
That's not it.

740
00:55:45,842 --> 00:55:48,303
Youjin just had surgery for appendicitis.

741
00:55:49,263 --> 00:55:52,015
Uh... So, she'll need
to take a few days off.

742
00:55:52,849 --> 00:55:55,227
Appendicitis?
She had her appendix removed?

743
00:55:55,310 --> 00:55:56,436
[Minjae] Yes.

744
00:55:59,565 --> 00:56:03,777
Well, she says she's okay,
and the surgery went well.

745
00:56:03,860 --> 00:56:05,028
So don't worry too much.

746
00:56:05,571 --> 00:56:08,073
-I'm glad to hear the surgery went well.
-[Minjae] Yeah.

747
00:56:08,615 --> 00:56:10,784
[clears throat] Well...

748
00:56:11,743 --> 00:56:14,871
These days, getting your appendix out
is hardly even surgery...

749
00:56:14,955 --> 00:56:18,166
Surgery is surgery. What do you mean,
it's hardly even surgery?

750
00:56:19,501 --> 00:56:20,544
Should we visit her?

751
00:56:21,086 --> 00:56:23,338
Apparently, they don't want any visitors.

752
00:56:24,548 --> 00:56:26,258
Well, they said not to come, so...

753
00:56:26,341 --> 00:56:28,802
But still, shouldn't we go check on her?

754
00:56:28,885 --> 00:56:31,930
But we'd just be bothering her
while she's recovering.

755
00:56:33,348 --> 00:56:35,309
No, there's no need to go. Don't worry.

756
00:58:46,481 --> 00:58:48,108
[Youjin] Professor Talking Hat?

757
00:58:52,112 --> 00:58:53,905
Why do you keep calling me "Talking Hat"?

758
00:58:56,283 --> 00:58:59,995
So, things ended with the ring guy?

759
00:59:04,166 --> 00:59:06,168
So all that going back and forth
was for nothing.

760
00:59:06,668 --> 00:59:08,545
I still don't get it.

761
00:59:10,130 --> 00:59:11,965
When did things start going wrong?

762
00:59:13,133 --> 00:59:14,760
It was all wrong from the start.

763
00:59:15,635 --> 00:59:18,138
Getting involved with a loser
was your first mistake.

764
00:59:21,099 --> 00:59:24,227
Good-looking guys
always come with a catch.

765
00:59:25,479 --> 00:59:26,521
Except me.

766
00:59:27,689 --> 00:59:29,149
[clicks tongue] Okay.

767
00:59:31,485 --> 00:59:33,987
There are plenty of guys out there.
Just find a new one.

768
00:59:35,447 --> 00:59:36,448
Okay.

769
00:59:38,575 --> 00:59:42,746
But is there really no other way?

770
00:59:42,829 --> 00:59:44,080
Professor Talking Hat?

771
00:59:47,042 --> 00:59:49,169
I'm not saying
I want to make it work with him.

772
00:59:50,337 --> 00:59:52,464
But we're going to keep seeing each other,

773
00:59:53,882 --> 00:59:55,258
so I want to clear the air.

774
00:59:56,134 --> 00:59:57,886
Still persistent after that rejection?

775
00:59:58,470 --> 00:59:59,721
I'm not being persistent.

776
01:00:01,181 --> 01:00:03,975
I just want to make him feel better
and more at ease.

777
01:00:05,936 --> 01:00:07,229
But I don't know how.

778
01:00:09,481 --> 01:00:12,609
[tuts] Will it work itself out with time?

779
01:00:12,692 --> 01:00:14,861
Isn't there anything else I can do?

780
01:00:14,945 --> 01:00:17,364
[Jihoon] You're stuck because
you're solving the wrong problem.

781
01:00:18,698 --> 01:00:19,699
Pardon?

782
01:00:20,325 --> 01:00:23,078
Whether he's angry or hurting,
he must figure it out himself.

783
01:00:23,161 --> 01:00:25,372
That's Minjae's problem to solve,
not yours.

784
01:00:27,666 --> 01:00:30,627
Find your own problem,
then find the answer to that problem.

785
01:00:35,882 --> 01:00:36,883
[Youjin] Huh?

786
01:00:38,301 --> 01:00:39,553
But why did you run away?

787
01:00:40,554 --> 01:00:41,555
What?

788
01:00:45,016 --> 01:00:46,351
I don't know.

789
01:00:46,434 --> 01:00:48,019
[Jihoon] You're lying. I know you do.

790
01:00:51,898 --> 01:00:53,024
You like him,

791
01:00:54,484 --> 01:00:56,361
but you didn't want to face his scar.

792
01:00:59,781 --> 01:01:04,119
Was the scar on his leg or in his heart?

793
01:01:05,787 --> 01:01:10,333
Was it in his past, present, or future?

794
01:01:13,545 --> 01:01:15,714
I'm not sure what you mean.

795
01:01:16,298 --> 01:01:19,009
Exactly. I feel like
I'm talking to a monkey right now.

796
01:01:22,554 --> 01:01:24,806
-What are you looking at?
-I'm just looking.

797
01:01:26,641 --> 01:01:28,685
[snickers] Fine. You're sick,
so I'll let it slide this time.

798
01:01:29,436 --> 01:01:30,562
Any more questions?

799
01:01:31,104 --> 01:01:32,522
I'm never taking your class.

800
01:01:32,606 --> 01:01:34,232
Take it. I'll give you good grades.

801
01:01:34,316 --> 01:01:35,734
A monkey can't get good grades.

802
01:01:35,817 --> 01:01:37,986
All my students are monkeys anyway.

803
01:01:42,073 --> 01:01:43,867
Please keep today's chat between us.

804
01:01:43,950 --> 01:01:44,951
It's a secret.

805
01:01:45,035 --> 01:01:46,953
You're the one who blurted it all out.

806
01:01:47,704 --> 01:01:50,081
You saved my life, so I trusted you.

807
01:01:52,834 --> 01:01:54,044
I saved your life?

808
01:01:55,003 --> 01:01:56,254
Watch your mouth.

809
01:01:56,338 --> 01:01:58,381
Don't make me kill someone
who saved my life.

810
01:02:00,133 --> 01:02:02,093
[Jihoon] I don't think
you're allowed to eat in here.

811
01:02:03,345 --> 01:02:06,556
[Youjin] Right. I'm not a student here.

812
01:02:08,725 --> 01:02:09,893
I'm a graduate.

813
01:02:10,852 --> 01:02:12,771
No one can hold my grades over my head

814
01:02:14,022 --> 01:02:16,816
or stop me from graduating,
so I can do whatever I want.

815
01:02:18,443 --> 01:02:19,986
Do you really not remember me?

816
01:02:21,488 --> 01:02:22,530
What?

817
01:02:23,073 --> 01:02:24,199
Never mind. Forget it.

818
01:03:28,471 --> 01:03:29,472
[Youjin] Minjae.

819
01:03:32,100 --> 01:03:33,476
-Minjae.
-What?

820
01:03:33,977 --> 01:03:35,520
What? What happened?

821
01:03:35,603 --> 01:03:37,230
I thought you were in the hospital.

822
01:03:37,814 --> 01:03:40,150
[Youjin] They don't keep you long
after an appendectomy.

823
01:03:40,233 --> 01:03:42,152
Well, then you should be resting at home.

824
01:03:42,235 --> 01:03:43,361
What are you doing here?

825
01:03:44,487 --> 01:03:47,490
[Youjin] I have something to tell you,
and something to show you.

826
01:03:48,533 --> 01:03:51,202
Really? Then can you wait here?
I'll go grab my phone.

827
01:03:51,286 --> 01:03:53,788
Actually, I'd rather talk at your place.

828
01:03:53,872 --> 01:03:55,665
-[Minjae] What?
-[Youjin] I have something to show you.

829
01:03:56,374 --> 01:03:58,251
You can show me right here. Let me see.

830
01:03:58,334 --> 01:03:59,377
I can't.

831
01:04:00,128 --> 01:04:01,379
Not in public.

832
01:04:02,255 --> 01:04:03,256
[Minjae] Why?

833
01:04:03,339 --> 01:04:04,340
I just can't.

834
01:04:05,467 --> 01:04:09,721
Uh, I don't know what it is,
but I can't let you in right now.

835
01:04:10,805 --> 01:04:13,141
Just show me at school later. Bye.

836
01:04:13,224 --> 01:04:16,352
If you won't let me in,
I'll just keep standing here.

837
01:04:16,978 --> 01:04:18,438
[Minjae] Okay, stand there forever then.

838
01:04:18,521 --> 01:04:19,981
-But...
-[Minjae] Wait.

839
01:04:20,065 --> 01:04:21,775
How did you know where I live?

840
01:04:23,359 --> 01:04:25,195
I asked Kim Sejin.

841
01:04:26,863 --> 01:04:27,864
Kim Sejin?

842
01:04:32,077 --> 01:04:33,078
[Youjin] Why?

843
01:04:40,376 --> 01:04:41,377
Okay. Come in.

844
01:04:42,670 --> 01:04:43,671
Yeah.

845
01:04:47,467 --> 01:04:50,136
You can go
and sit on the couch over there.

846
01:04:50,220 --> 01:04:51,221
[Youjin] Okay.

847
01:04:51,304 --> 01:04:52,722
[Minjae groaning] Just give me a second.

848
01:05:10,865 --> 01:05:11,866
Uh...

849
01:05:13,868 --> 01:05:18,331
By the way, I think water is all I've got.

850
01:05:18,414 --> 01:05:20,166
Do you want some? Is that okay?

851
01:05:20,250 --> 01:05:21,251
[Youjin] Yes.

852
01:05:24,546 --> 01:05:26,256
-[Minjae] Here.
-Thank you.

853
01:05:35,223 --> 01:05:38,143
You said you had something to show me.
So show me, then go.

854
01:05:52,115 --> 01:05:53,324
What are you doing?

855
01:05:53,408 --> 01:05:55,118
I need to take this off first.

856
01:05:55,201 --> 01:05:56,369
[Minjae] Take it off? Why?

857
01:05:56,452 --> 01:05:58,288
What are you doing?
Are you out of your mind?

858
01:06:00,498 --> 01:06:02,750
Come on, look.

859
01:06:02,834 --> 01:06:04,210
Hey, Lim Youjin.

860
01:06:04,294 --> 01:06:06,880
This isn't going to work on me.
I'm not giving in.

861
01:06:06,963 --> 01:06:08,089
Not a chance.

862
01:06:08,173 --> 01:06:10,425
Don't take your clothes off.
Put them back on.

863
01:06:11,593 --> 01:06:13,970
[Youjin sighs, mumbles] Just look.

864
01:06:14,053 --> 01:06:16,306
No, I'm not looking.

865
01:06:17,307 --> 01:06:19,684
If you keep this up,
I'm calling the cops, okay?

866
01:06:20,852 --> 01:06:22,854
Don't get the wrong idea. Just look.

867
01:06:22,937 --> 01:06:23,938
No.

868
01:06:24,022 --> 01:06:25,815
Look at where I had surgery.

869
01:06:35,783 --> 01:06:39,704
[Minjae] Hey, why are you taking that off?
What if it gets infected? Put it back on.

870
01:06:40,955 --> 01:06:42,665
-[Youjin] Look at it.
-[Minjae sighs wearily]

871
01:06:44,125 --> 01:06:48,296
I guess I can't wear a bikini anymore
with this scar, right?

872
01:06:49,464 --> 01:06:50,798
[mumbling] What?

873
01:06:50,882 --> 01:06:52,342
You were going to wear a bikini?

874
01:06:52,425 --> 01:06:54,761
Guys all love bikinis, don't they?

875
01:06:55,887 --> 01:06:57,972
Hey, the bikini's not the problem.

876
01:06:58,056 --> 01:07:00,642
[groans] This... It must've hurt so much.

877
01:07:02,227 --> 01:07:03,811
[Youjin] The surgery didn't hurt.

878
01:07:03,895 --> 01:07:05,063
I was put under.

879
01:07:06,105 --> 01:07:09,067
It still hurts,
even if they put you under. [groans]

880
01:07:10,902 --> 01:07:13,029
[Youjin] Now stop looking.
I'm getting embarrassed.

881
01:07:13,571 --> 01:07:14,656
-[Minjae] Sorry.
-[Youjin] Okay.

882
01:07:22,455 --> 01:07:25,583
Now that you've seen mine,
show me yours too.

883
01:07:27,377 --> 01:07:28,378
What?

884
01:07:29,712 --> 01:07:31,965
Show me where they operated on your leg.

885
01:07:35,093 --> 01:07:36,511
You can't just look at mine.

886
01:07:37,136 --> 01:07:39,389
Show me yours too, so we're even.

887
01:07:43,476 --> 01:07:44,727
Show me yours too.

888
01:07:46,604 --> 01:07:48,481
I'm not going home until you show me.

889
01:07:50,108 --> 01:07:51,150
Look at you.

890
01:07:58,366 --> 01:08:00,410
[scoffing] Jeez. Fine, look.

891
01:08:00,493 --> 01:08:02,829
I'll show you. Go on and look.

892
01:08:24,058 --> 01:08:25,059
Look.

893
01:08:31,065 --> 01:08:32,358
Can I touch it?

894
01:08:32,859 --> 01:08:33,860
What?

895
01:08:35,862 --> 01:08:36,863
You can touch it.

896
01:08:40,742 --> 01:08:41,743
[Youjin] Did that hurt?

897
01:08:42,493 --> 01:08:43,661
No, I'm just surprised.

898
01:08:44,412 --> 01:08:45,621
It doesn't hurt anymore.

899
01:08:47,248 --> 01:08:50,376
But it must've hurt a lot
when you had the surgery.

900
01:08:51,711 --> 01:08:53,296
It didn't hurt. I was put under.

901
01:08:54,380 --> 01:08:55,423
That's a lie.

902
01:08:56,674 --> 01:08:58,176
You think I'm an idiot?

903
01:08:59,093 --> 01:09:01,512
Even a tiny paper cut hurts so much.

904
01:09:06,225 --> 01:09:07,977
[softly] It must've hurt so much.

905
01:09:09,562 --> 01:09:12,148
It must've hurt so much.
[voice breaking] It must have...

906
01:09:21,240 --> 01:09:22,825
[sobbing] It must've hurt so much.

907
01:09:26,204 --> 01:09:27,747
Hey, are you crying?

908
01:09:29,290 --> 01:09:30,708
Hey, don't be like this.

909
01:09:30,792 --> 01:09:31,793
Stand up.

910
01:09:31,876 --> 01:09:34,170
[Youjin sobs] Why did you have to go
and get sick like that?

911
01:09:35,171 --> 01:09:37,131
Everyone else is doing just fine.

912
01:09:37,632 --> 01:09:39,384
What makes you so special, huh?

913
01:09:40,718 --> 01:09:43,221
Everyone else...
Everyone else is perfectly healthy,

914
01:09:43,304 --> 01:09:46,432
so why did you have
to get a disease like that? Why?

915
01:09:52,855 --> 01:09:54,482
It must've hurt so much.

916
01:09:56,150 --> 01:09:57,902
God, this is annoying.

917
01:09:57,985 --> 01:09:59,696
This is annoying. [cries]

918
01:10:01,197 --> 01:10:02,907
[sniffles] This is annoying...

919
01:10:04,492 --> 01:10:05,827
[softly] Don't cry. Don't be like this.

920
01:10:05,910 --> 01:10:07,704
-Don't cry. Seriously.
-[Youjin sobbing]

921
01:10:11,666 --> 01:10:13,084
It hurt at the time.

922
01:10:14,293 --> 01:10:17,672
But it's all healed now, and I'm fine.
It doesn't hurt anymore.

923
01:10:25,430 --> 01:10:28,015
Stop and get up. Come on, get up.

924
01:10:33,312 --> 01:10:36,566
[loudly] Stop crying, for goodness' sake.
You're driving me crazy! Okay?

925
01:10:37,734 --> 01:10:39,110
Look at me. Open your eyes.

926
01:10:40,278 --> 01:10:41,446
Look at me!

927
01:10:44,365 --> 01:10:46,993
[softly] You need to look at me
so I can talk, you know.

928
01:10:47,869 --> 01:10:48,911
Look at me.

929
01:10:52,665 --> 01:10:53,750
I'm okay now.

930
01:10:56,627 --> 01:10:57,712
I'm not sick anymore.

931
01:10:59,464 --> 01:11:00,673
I'm fine.

932
01:12:02,068 --> 01:12:05,988
BETWEEN STEPS

933
01:12:06,531 --> 01:12:07,990
[Youjin] <i>I love coming to school.</i>

934
01:12:08,074 --> 01:12:09,992
<i>I always look forward to seeing you guys.</i>

935
01:12:10,827 --> 01:12:12,954
[Sejin] <i>What was Lim Youjin</i>
<i>doing at your place?</i>

936
01:12:13,037 --> 01:12:16,874
<i>Things can get really messy in a lab</i>
<i>when romance is involved.</i>

937
01:12:16,958 --> 01:12:19,627
<i>I'll nip this in the bud</i>
<i>before it causes any trouble.</i>

938
01:12:19,710 --> 01:12:20,878
Have you seen this?

939
01:12:20,962 --> 01:12:23,089
Lim Youjin,
why are you coming out so late?

940
01:12:23,172 --> 01:12:25,007
It's not like you're never coming back.

941
01:12:25,091 --> 01:12:26,634
I might never come back.

942
01:12:27,218 --> 01:12:28,427
I won't come back.

943
01:12:28,511 --> 01:12:29,929
[Youjin] You're such a coward.

944
01:12:30,012 --> 01:12:32,014
Stay that way for the rest of your life.
